  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minnesota has $1.5B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Minnesota recorded 24,832 awards with an average award size of $59.1K. Obligations fell 41.0% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Minnesota with $462M in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $251M and the Department of Agriculture with $243M. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION leads vendors with $185M, followed by MCGOUGH CONSTRUCTION CO., LLC with $106M and BAE SYSTEMS LAND & ARMAMENTS L.P. with $66.7M. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing is the single largest industry by obligations at $185M, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $126M and Cheese Manufacturing at $95M. FY21 through FY26 show variability: FY21 was $2.6B, FY22 was $2.4B, FY23 was $2.7B, FY24 was $3B, FY25 was $2.5B, and FY26 is $1.5B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers in Minnesota?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $462M in Minnesota for FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $251M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $243M. The General Services Administration and the Department of Health and Human Services follow with $142M and $126M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which companies and industries capture the most federal spending in Minnesota?",
        "body": "NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION received $185M, making it the largest vendor by obligations in FY2026 to date. MCGOUGH CONSTRUCTION CO., LLC and BAE SYSTEMS LAND & ARMAMENTS L.P. received $106M and $66.7M respectively. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing leads industries with $185M, while Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Cheese Manufacturing received $126M and $95M respectively."
      }
